Input: {"question": "When was the Howard County Courthouse built?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0477-3f0367c85491:d00", "start": 0, "end": 110, "text": "Howard County Courthouse (Iowa) The Howard County Courthouse in Cresco, Iowa, United States was built in 1880."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0477-3f0367c85491:d00", "start": 111, "end": 239, "text": "It was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1981 as a part of the County Courthouses in Iowa Thematic Resource."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0477-3f0367c85491:d00", "start": 240, "end": 343, "text": "The courthouse is the third building the county has used for court functions and county administration."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0477-3f0367c85491:d00", "start": 344, "end": 442, "text": "When Howard County was organized in 1855 the county judge named Vernon Springs as the county seat."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0477-3f0367c85491:d00", "start": 443, "end": 536, "text": "Later in the year he ordered that the court and all county records be moved to Howard Center."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0477-3f0367c85491:d00", "start": 537, "end": 587, "text": "New Oregon wanted the county seat there, but Pikes"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0477-3f0367c85491:d01", "start": 0, "end": 45, "text": "for Howard County Courthouse Location Elm St."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0477-3f0367c85491:d01", "start": 46, "end": 200, "text": "Cresco , Iowa Coordinates 43°22′26″N 92°7′3″W ﻿ / ﻿ 43.37389°N 92.11750°W ﻿ / 43.37389 ; -92.11750 Area less than one acre Built 1879-1880 Architect B.D ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0477-3f0367c85491:d01", "start": 201, "end": 217, "text": "Everingham J.L ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0477-3f0367c85491:d01", "start": 218, "end": 309, "tex